  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MAINSTREAM: Fair and Ethical Recruitment into the Philippines&#x2019; Migration Governance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 3 February 2022, the Department of Migrant Workers Act (Republic Act No. 1164) took effect, which established the Department of Migrant Workers and for the very first time in the world a country codified the progressive realization of the 23 Objectives of the Global Compact for Safe, Orderly and Regular Migration (GCM). The project aims to capitalize this momentous time to promote fair and ethical recruitment practices to government agencies, employers and Private Recruitment Agencies (PRAs) and to support the Philippine government in meeting key objectives in the multi-stakeholder National Action Plan on Mainstreaming Fair and Ethical Recruitment in the Philippines (NAP-FER), particularly on developing due diligence and self-assessment tools for the recruitment industry (Objective 3) and on implementing continuous capacity-building (Objective 4).</narrative>
  </description>
